        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qqbot): resolve start() when abort signal already fired",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where stopping the QQBot gateway during or immediately after startup could leave `GatewayConnection.start()` pending forever when the caller AbortSignal was already aborted. The previous lifecycle also continued connecting after an early abort, which could leave a socket created during shutdown outside cleanup ownership.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`start()` registered abort listeners after work had already begun without normalizing an already-fired signal. The fix makes abort handling idempotent at registration, skips connection work for pre-aborted starts, and checks lifecycle ownership after each asynchronous startup stage. A socket created after an in-flight abort is closed before it can be adopted. Risk is limited to the QQBot connection startup and shutdown path; no config or protocol surface changes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQQBot channel stop/restart no longer hangs when shutdown overlaps startup, and startup does not retain a WebSocket that finishes opening after its lifecycle owner has stopped.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Live configured-account proof (redacted):**\n\n```\ncredentialExchangeSucceeded: true\nabortPhase: after start invocation\noutcome: resolved\nelapsedMs: 146\nexistingGatewayLeftRunning: true\n```\n\nThis ran the exported `GatewayConnection` with the locally configured QQBot app ID and secret file, forced a fresh real QQ credential exchange, then aborted immediately after invoking `start()`. The patched lifecycle resolved in 146 ms after the real credential request and stopped before gateway URL/socket adoption. The already-running live Gateway was left online, and no messages were sent.\n\n**Deterministic before proof on the original implementation:**\n\n```\nlabel: before-fix\ntimedOut: true\nelapsedMs: 501\nresolved: false\nexit: 1\n```\n\nThe same exported-class harness with a pre-aborted signal exceeded its 500 ms bound before the fix.\n\n**Focused regression tests:**\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qqbot/src/engine/gateway/gateway-connection.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       9 passed (9)\n```\n\nCoverage now verifies both that a pre-aborted start performs no socket creation and that a socket returned after an in-flight abort is immediately closed.\n\n**Additional checks:**\n\n```\n$ pnpm format extensions/qqbot/src/engine/gateway/gateway-connection.ts extensions/qqbot/src/engine/gateway/gateway-connection.test.ts\nFinished on 2 files\n\n$ git diff --check\n# clean\n```\n\n`pnpm check:changed` attempted to delegate its heavy lane to unavailable maintainer Testbox infrastructure and exited before running the remote check. Full type/lint/build gates are therefore left to GitHub Actions. A full active-service restart was not performed because it would disrupt the existing live channel.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex and Cursor; proof runs executed on this machine.",
